# Grants the app's own user passwordless sudo for exactly two commands --
# nothing broader:
#   - rebooting the host (Device Stats page's "Reboot device" button)
#   - restarting the API service itself (used after a database restore, so
#     the process reopens the swapped-in file with a clean connection)
# Install with:
#   sudo install -m 0440 hamstation-system-sudoers /etc/sudoers.d/hamstation-system
# then validate with `sudo visudo -c` before trusting it.
__APP_USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl reboot
__APP_USER__ ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl restart --no-block hamstation-api
